{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system","id":1195582,"title":"Archmage: The Seeking 2E (Homebrew System)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-14T19:31:09-07:00","id":1195582,"title":"Archmage: The Seeking 2E (Homebrew System)","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">[Ths post is a <i>work in progress</i>: expect multiple edits and additions over the next few weeks. Comments, suggestions, contributions, etc. are welcomed and appreciated!] </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Archmage: The Seeking</span></span></u></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;I once received a black belt. In that moment, I felt that I mastered my craft. Only later did I find that it was not the end of learning, but the true beginning. Only a master can perceive that fact. You are a Master, as well - one who, Awake, dreamed he was awake. The difference between what you were and what you are becoming is the difference between Earth and Heaven. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">You are Awakening - again. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The worlds are now dust and nations, which will flourish with your joy and reel with your pain. Your allies will be a constant threat, your enemies the only ones who can understand you. The weak will come to lean on you. The lepers will call you Lord. And all will seek your wise counsel. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">But knowledge is cruel. It will break your heart and test your allegiances. Are you certain you want this curse?&quot; </span></span></i><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Oreus, Paragon of the Adamantine Arrow</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Archmage Basics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">(Note: Archmages are far too potent to use in a normal World of Darkness game hosting default templates, such as Mage or Vampire. They are designed as Greater Beings - as such, Archmages should not be PCs without prior knowledge and consent from all players involved.) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Archmage's souls cannot be tampered with or destroyed</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Archmages automatically win Clash of Wills in all scenarios except against Greater Beings (entities with both Power Stat [Blood Potency, Primal Urge, Gnosis, etc...] and Template Abilities [i.e. Disciplines, Gifts, Supernal Magic, etc] at 6+ dots). Against Greater Beings, CoW functions normally.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Archmage's spells are immune to being counterspelled or dispelled by anything except other Archmages (and Greater Beings when applicable)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Archmages no longer follow a Path; they rather forge their own trail to the Supernal called the Golden Road. As such, they treat all Arcana as Ruling.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*When an Archmage physically dies in the any reality which qualifies as &quot;part of &quot;The Lie,&quot; she is immediately transported to the entrance of her Golden Road (or Chantry, or any spot previously designated as a &quot;respawn point&quot;) with the &quot;Soul Shocked&quot; condition. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Access to Imperial Magic, also known as Higher Practices. These use a new Imperial Factor chart, and are always Ritually Cast.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Archmages study what they call Concepts: in practice, these are &quot;tiers&quot; of magic that each have two &quot;Interdisciplinaries&quot; (sub-sections). The following is information gleaned regarding these Concepts, and the Interdisciplinaries they contain.<br /> <br /> Please note that the following examples are merely suggestions. The full possibilities of each Interdisciplinary - and the Concept that rules them - are far more numerous than what this post can possibly list. Truly, Archmages are unharnessed from lists of specifics: creativity and planning, necessity and experimentation make each Concept a world unto itself, and as such virtually unlimited in scope within their purview. (The only exception is the Interdisciplinary of Proficiency, which by its nature a finite (yet potent!) list of improvements. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Arcanum 6 Dots </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Concept of Intrinsics (Themes: Completion and Initiation)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Interdisciplinary of Proficiency </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The first thing a new Archmage does is cement her mastery of the Common Practices. Each benefit is studied and purchased separately.<br /> Note that all the following benefits of Proficiency apply to Arcanum Dots 1-5 only. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Among the benefits of Proficiency: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Unlimited, free Reach</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Ritual Casting becomes Instant Casting (Spells can still be Ritually Cast, but the process is instant.) </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Common Practices no longer invoke Paradox</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*An Exceptional Success on a spellcast may evoke all benefits available to such </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Common Practices no longer cost mana </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*All Common Practices can be cast at Intimate Sympathetic/Temporal connection (not knowing True Name still reduces level of connection by 1; applies to &quot;Lesser Beings&quot; only)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Rotes and Praxises of Common Practices may be combined </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Any number of Yantras may be applied as a Reflexive action </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Interdisciplinary of Dynamics</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Archmage has her first taste of Imperial Magic. These spells are examples of the precept that Magic is Alive.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Among the benefits of Dynamics:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Spells that adapt and evolve, having a base intelligence and will of their own </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Shielding spells that adapt to the current threat</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Spells that are passed like a disease or idea from target-to-target </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Spells that can cast spells </span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;I once met a Seeker who slew Luna herself. It was a titanic battle, that lasted several days in Fallen time. It was the most gratituous thing</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I've ever heard of -- I suspect he did it just to prove he could. Luna didn't stay dead for long, mind you; her patronage saw to that. But </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">that Seeker is now considered a danger, unstable. His reputation took more damage than what it gained. The Pax falls hard on hubris.&quot; </span></span></i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Arcanum 7 Dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Concept of Establishment (Themes: Creation and Sundering)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Archmage has reached a level of power that allows her to transform what exists in accordance to her will. She can manipulate The Lie, herself, and other beings in impossible, wonderful ways.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Interdisciplinary of Evocations </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Shape the Soul, creating Chanties and Ochemata </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Modify template of self, adding to what exists</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Modify templates of other beings, adding to what exists</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Add multiple Legacies </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Interdisciplinary of Excisions </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Modify Template of self, removing unwanted qualities </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Modify Template of others, removing unwanted qualities </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Arcanum 8 Dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Concept of Metamorphoses (Themes: Conceptualization and Oblivion; Imagination Made Real, The Real Made Into Imagination)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Archmage has finally reached the cusp of godhood. At this level, the rules of reality can be rewritten wholesale. If &quot;Establishment&quot; is like the Common Practice of Weaving, &quot;Metamorphoses&quot; is the equivalent of Making/Unmaking - unshackled of concepts such as &quot;possible&quot; or &quot;real.&quot; </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Interdisciplary of Incitements </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Grossly modify the template of herself: create new rules, increase limits of Gnosis/Arcana/Mana </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Grossly modify the template of others: create new rules, increase the limites of Gnosis/Arcana/Mana (or equivilents of other Templates)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Interdisciplinary of Extirpations<br /> *Remove aspects of reality of the self at a dramatic level, removing the ability to die or take physical damage<br /> *Unmake aspects of reality of others beings, and the world, at a dramatic level, removing the ability to cause harm, think, form Imagos, use<br /> template resources, or innate weaknesses<br /> *Remove the ability to activate or utilize abilities<br /> *Remove something or someone's existence at a fundamental level</span></span><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;Leovold has several Ochema, perfect clones down to the birth mark on his ass and free will. Well, turns out that some random upstart - no offense - lured </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">one into his sanctum under some false pretense, and somehow managed to kill him. Now Leovold is claiming he was murdered. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Some are sympathetic to his claims -- hell, at this point it's hard to say Leovold isn't just as much his Ochema as he is himself. Others say he is playing a rhetorical game, playing the victim for sympathy from his peers. The case has garnered quite a following.&quot; </span></span></i><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Arcanum 9 Dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Concept of Incarnations (Contained Omniscience)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The next logical step from Metamorphoses is to seek a way to more readily access the power it grants. The Interdisciplinaries of Incarnations are both Quintessences, which combine to give the Archmage a scene's worth of time to freely cast Imperial Magic, up to and including Metamorphoses-tier Supernal Magic. The only caveat is that a spell cannot be cast to make this effect permanent: if that is accomplished, it is the logical equivelant of Ascension. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-The interdisciplinary of Selves</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-The interdisciplinary of [X Arcanum] </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">When combined, grants access to this state-of-being<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;I drank your nectar, Beloved<br /> and grew in radiance. Now,<br /> emanating your sweet fragrance,<br /> even the Angel of Death has no hope.&quot;</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Arcanum 10 Dots</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Concept of Ascensions </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The state of &quot;Incarnations&quot; made permanent. The Archmage ascends. This is one possible route. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-Interdisciplinary of Representations</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A quintessence which represents the state of the Archmaster and the Arcana used becoming one. Rumored to be attainable while in the elevated state of Incarnations itself. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">-The interdisciplinary of Eternities<br /> A quintessence which represents permanence of power. Finding this quintessence is a true test for any Archmage. One can never prepare for it. It can only be<br /> obtained through a method unique to each individual. Often, this is the ultimate expression of mastery: a challenge so tailored to the individual that any attempt to aid another in obtaining this quintessence automatically fails. <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;THE ESSENCE .. OF<br /> EVERY THOUG HT...........EVERY SPELL,<br /> EVERY<br /> WORLD,<br /> IS POWER. NO<br /> THING ELS E </i></span></span><br /> <i>MATTERS<br /> BEC<br /> AUSE NOTHING ELSE<br /> EXISTS&quot;</i><br /> -Artaes, The Mad Fulcrum<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">[Edits and additional content to come!]</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 03-15-2018, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T19:48:28-07:00","id":1195591,"title":"","content":"While we all know archmages are often literally playing a different game, isn\u2019t this a bit too different from what we know of 1E stuff?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Of course, that doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s bad. Just unexpected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T20:33:55-07:00","id":1195600,"title":"","content":"That's a fair observation. In what ways do you feel it's too different?<br /> <br /> I guess I feel that a dramatic Second Awakening should contain sharp difference, while still maintaining the spirit of Mage: The Awakening. I don't want difference for the sake of being different, though. I'm genuinely trying to strike a balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T21:14:01-07:00","id":1195608,"title":"","content":"Can I ask what the main objective is for your re-write?<br /> Mainly my question is why ditch what we've already got from Imperial Mysteries.<br /> Without knowing what you're shooting for, a lot of the changes seem completely arbitrary.<br /> <br /> Knowing what you want to get out of your homebrew will make it easier for people to comment.<br /> I mean, apart from making it 2e-compatible, Imperial Mysteries is sufficiently rules-light to make it easy enough to represent the Imperial Practices.<br /> <br /> Also I would STRONGLY suggest never offering Infinite Reach as a universal spell option.<br /> That offers infinite spells, and removes the largest source Paradox dice in the game.<br /> And given your Gnosis will be 6+, that's a lot of dice you're throwing away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T21:35:33-07:00","id":1195616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system?p=1195600#post1195600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a fair observation. In what ways do you feel it's too different?<br /> <br /> I guess I feel that a dramatic Second Awakening should contain sharp difference, while still maintaining the spirit of Mage: The Awakening. I don't want difference for the sake of being different, though. I'm genuinely trying to strike a balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Concepts and Interdisciplinaries. I assume Concepts are, well, concepts, but what are the latter in lay-mage\u2019s terms? Practices? Attainments? Quintessences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T21:38:36-07:00","id":1195617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can I ask what the main objective is for your re-write? </div> </div> </div>I recently read DaveB (author of Imperial Mysteries, for those who don't know) say something to the effect of &quot;Imperial Mysteries is out-dated, and much of it is no longer compatible with Mage 2E.&quot; I'm paraphrasing, and I don't want to misrepresent DaveB - but I do agree with that sentiment. Archmage is something that has always caught my interest, and I think making it more compatible with Mage 2E is not only great fun, but also opens up opportunity for new gameplay. It's my pet, passion project. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I would STRONGLY suggest never offering Infinite Reach as a universal spell option.<br /> That offers infinite spells, and removes the largest source Paradox dice in the game. </div> </div> </div>I'm not 100% sure if you're aware of not, which is why I'm repeating it... <br /> but the Paradox-free casting only applies to the &quot;Common Practices&quot; i.e. Arcanum magic of 1-5 dots. <br /> <br /> Anything 6+ dots, and/or any magic that draws upon the Imperial Spells Factors (not yet included, but I'll be adding it) DOES INDEED invoke Paradox - and containment makes the Archmage take *lethal, resistant* damage. Paradox-free magic applies to the Common Practices using the standard spell factor chart only. It's part of the Interdisciplinary of Proficiency, which can be summed up as &quot;mastery of the old.&quot; <br /> <br /> I drew inspiration for the &quot;unlimited free Reach&quot; idea from the Core 2E books itself! While not explicitly stated, it is implied that Archmasters can cast common-level (not Imperial/Imperially-altered) magic extremely freely, at a Platonically ideal sense. <br /> <br /> Supernal Magic is essentially perfection, and the Awakened will is a conduit for it, This is why Exceptional Successes are a - stay with me haha - perfect expression of perfection. When an Archmage casts the Common Practices, my logic is that Reach introduces the possibility of a flawed representation of perfection. Archmages don't have that problem with the <i>Common Practices - </i>therefore Reach isn't posing an issue like it does to the ranks of merely Awakened Mages. <br /> <br /> I think it bears repeating once more, that this free Reach is limited to the Common Practices only; unmodified by Imperial alterations. Such is their mastery of the old. <br /> When dealing with &quot;the new&quot; e.g. casting Imperial Magic, Paradox is even more lethal and prevalent than ever before (at least, until the Archmage in question reaches both Metamorphoses AND has the tools to deal with Paradox alteration (likely 8 dots in Prime). <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T21:58:16-07:00","id":1195624,"title":"","content":"DaveB's mostly mentioned that the spellcasting system is outdated, as well as several aspects of the setting (I'm looking at you, Old Gods of the Thistle).<br /> I really don't see what benefit there is in tearing up those old roots to make new ones from scratch.<br /> <br /> Also I really, really wouldn't suggest 'unlocking' some of the basic elements of spellcasting to make them more 'perfect'.<br /> Unlimited free reach on all non-Imperial Practices, immunity to Paradox, Ritual Casting at turn-interval speed, using all Yantras in one reflexive.<br /> You might as well throw the base spellcasting system out of the window.<br /> <br /> Also that infinite reach was reserved for certain spells while standing in a Demesne, and for Supernal Entities, who can only use it for very limited Arcana, and are literally the Supernal made manifest.<br /> At the very least restrict those benefits to whatever Arcanum you've reached Archmastery levels with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T22:32:51-07:00","id":1195629,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of things I disagree with in this design. I'll agree with the benefits given to sub-imperial sorcery being overpowered in a rather uninteresting way. I'll also comment that the introduced terminology of Interdisciplinaries is opaque, unintuitive, and generally kind of clunky-sounding. Mostly, though, I just wanted to poke in briefly to highlight something that randomly struck my attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system#post1195582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">*Archmages automatically win Clash of Wills in all scenarios except against Greater Beings (entities with both Power Stat [Blood Potency, Primal Urge, Gnosis, etc...] and Template Abilities [i.e. Disciplines, Gifts, Supernal Magic, etc] at 6+ dots). Against Greater Beings, CoW functions normally.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a great metric to measure whether a character is competing at a comparable level. For one, there are no Template Abilities I'm aware of (off the top of my head, at least) that exceed a five-dot rating except for the Arcana themselves. Many templates <i>don't even use dot ratings</i> for their core abilities at all (Prometheans, Changelings, Mummies, Demons, and Beasts!). I would honestly not try to make an ironclad mechanical definition here, and just give some suitable examples of what you would consider Greater Beings for these purposes. Ephemeral entities of high enough Rank to manifest Royal Avatars are a likely inclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T22:39:52-07:00","id":1195631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system?p=1195616#post1195616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Concepts and Interdisciplinaries. I assume Concepts are, well, concepts, but what are the latter in lay-mage\u2019s terms? Practices? Attainments? Quintessences?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good question. The simple way I can describe Interdisciplinaries are a mix between Practices (weaving, unmaking, etc) and Attainments.<br /> <br /> They are different, new ways of applying magic. The &quot;Concept&quot; is the Practice (Making/Unmaking for example, but described in one word), and the Interdisciplinary is the subdivision (Making = Procifiencies, Unmaking = Dynamics). That's an example, as Unmaking and Dynamics aren't functionally the same, neither is Making and Proficiencies.<br /> <br /> In order to master the Concept and move on, one must master both its subdivisions -- the Concept of Intrinsics contains both subdivisions of &quot;Proficiencies&quot; AND &quot;Dynamics.&quot; Once both Interdisciplinaries (i.e. subdivisions) are completely purchased via XP, the Archmage can move on to a new Concept. which also contains two Interdisciplinaries (subdivisions). And so on...<br /> <br /> It would be like renaming a Master of Life<br /> as a student of the Concept of Creations<br /> with Interdisciplinaries of &quot;Healings&quot; and &quot;Transformations&quot;<br /> <br /> Now the Life arcanum is far more broad that just those two abilities. BUT Archmages no longer study a particular Arcanum as much as they study NEW WAYS TO USE IT.<br /> Therefore, Concepts is the sweeping term, the label - the Interdisciplinaries are two (generally opposite) ways of applying that Concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the very least restrict those benefits to whatever Arcanum you've reached Archmastery levels with. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry that I didn't make this more clear, but that is already the case. The Interdisciplinary of Proficiencies only applies to Arcana that you've reached 6 dots in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also that infinite reach was reserved for certain spells while standing in a Demesne, and for Supernal Entities, who can only use it for very limited Arcana, and are literally the Supernal made manifest. </div> </div> </div>Archmages travel to the Supernal Realm that corresponds to the Arcanum they've reached Archmastery in, and must make it back alive in order to become an Archmage. One could make a very strong case that they are, in a very real sense, now a Supernal Entity - albeit in human form.<br /> They aren't Saint Michael so much as Jesus Christ - but they are still very much &quot;other.&quot; Archmastery is a second Awakening; as such, they are now far past the limits of not only Mages, but lesser supernatural beings in general. The are &quot;Greater Beings&quot; with all that entails.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do think I understand your concerns, and I genuinely appreciate your input. You bring up valid concerns. I'd like to hear more from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 03-15-2018, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-14T22:57:51-07:00","id":1195634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">This is not a great metric to measure whether a character is competing at a comparable level. For one, there are no Template Abilities I'm aware of (off the top of my head, at least) that exceed a five-dot rating except for the Arcana themselves. Many templates <i>don't even use dot ratings</i> for their core abilities at all (Prometheans, Changelings, Mummies, Demons, and Beasts!). I would honestly not try to make an ironclad mechanical definition here, and just give some suitable examples of what you would consider Greater Beings for these purposes. Ephemeral entities of high enough Rank to manifest Royal Avatars are a likely inclusion.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>We're just going to have to disagree with the contents of your first paragraph, without getting into the details. What is unintuitive and &quot;clunky-sounding&quot; to one person is elegant and refined to another. And as for overpowered &quot;sub-imperial sorcery&quot; - well, yeah, Archmages are overpowered. So that's not really a concern of mine. They don't need to be overpowered in an interesting way, either, when it comes to the Common Practices: this is the end flourishes of the system they are departing; the primary work lies ahead. The mission isn't to rework the Common Practices in a new and exciting way. It is to begin to add new and exciting abilities. The Interdisciplinary of Proficiencies is merely one subdivision of 5 new Concepts, 1/10th of the new mechanical content. Creating mastery of the old is using the old in better ways. But they are still the old ways. Far better lies ahead than what they leave behind.<br /> <br /> But I mainly wanted to address the quote above. I included a metric <i>exactly because </i>there are no template abilities that exceed 5 dots, except for Supernal Magic.<br /> When not applicable, simply assume the following: unless the template DOES have template abilities above 5, it is not a greater being.<br /> Promethians, Changelings, Mummies, Demons, and Beasts are not Greater Beings.<br /> <br /> Deathlords, True Fae, Spirits Rank 5+, Archangels are Greater Beings by caveat. Anything else is a no-go, unless they hit the requirements.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 03-15-2018, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T01:41:17-07:00","id":1195655,"title":"","content":"Aww, but what about hunter-bodhisattvas whose Renown don\u2019t necessarily go up to 6+? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyways, speaking of Werewolf and reading some of the lore parts up there... Luna, killed? And backed by a patron? That\u2019s quite a big setting change, since for the most part Luna <i>is</i> one of such \u2018greater patrons.\u2019 What do you have in mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T05:37:41-07:00","id":1195690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system?p=1195634#post1195634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promethians, Changelings, Mummies, Demons, and Beasts are not Greater Beings.<br /> <br /> Deathlords, True Fae, Spirits Rank 5+, Archangels are Greater Beings by caveat. Anything else is a no-go, unless they hit the requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's.... dreadfully arbitrary. You have just listed one of the strongest beings in the setting with one of the weakest. Most of the Greater Beings you talk about are totally unplayable in any way- and I'm talking about ST level playability. How to you present solid mechanics to things like the Judges? How do you write down vampire's Blood Gods or Chthonic Gods? You could style them all as high Ranked spirits, but it kinda miss the point IMO. Half of what you describe as Greater Beings has no mechanics in the new edition, so you can't actually fight them in the first place- and trying to force the design of one game on others to decide what is a Greater Being feels, well, <i>wrong</i>. And yeah, Luna being casually killed (a spirit of Rank 8-9 if I'm not mistaken) is not something any archmaster could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T14:57:00-07:00","id":1195856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the Greater Beings you talk about are totally unplayable in any way- and I'm talking about ST level playability. </div> </div> </div>Every being I listed is able to be played by an ST. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do you write down vampire's Blood Gods or Chthonic Gods? </div> </div> </div>That varies from ST to ST, and you're making quite a stretch to even assume they exist. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> And yeah, Luna being casually killed (a spirit of Rank 8-9 if I'm not mistaken) is not something any archmaster could do. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><br /> <br /> &quot;Casually killed&quot; <br /> &quot;A titanic battle that lasted several days...&quot; <br /> <br /> If you're trying to say an Archmage <i>could ever</i> become more powerful than a Rank 8 Spirit, I suggest reviewing Imperial Mysteries.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:42:03-07:00","id":1195873,"title":"","content":"A Scion born of Zeus, in the titular game, could ever become powerful enough to slay Optimus Maximum himself. A Solar in Exalted could (and in the past, have) become powerful enough to take on the Celestial Incarnae themselves. That\u2019s... still not going to convince people that a background character did once before, and that Zeus or the Incarnae got resurrected by a mysterious higher power.<br /> <br /> I see it something like what applies to normal mages: A mage is in theory, and mages as a species, can take on some of the strongest (but still below archmaster-tier) beings. In practice, such are feats of legend are reserved for only the mightiest and bloody-determined of them all. Archmages taking on gods being similar; they can grow to do just that (espcially at Arcanum 9-10), but that\u2019s not going to be common. <br /> <br /> The Luna-got-slain-once episode sounds casual not because of what the archmaster did, but because it\u2019s presented in a way that makes it sound a typical, expected feat for archmages at that level. <br /> <br /> Unless, of course, this all was your intention. Then it\u2019s fair game as long as you make it all self-consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:33:34-07:00","id":1195893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system?p=1195856#post1195856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're trying to say an Archmage <i>could ever</i> become more powerful than a Rank 8 Spirit, I suggest reviewing Imperial Mysteries.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's the way you placed it next to the 6th dot. That makes it look like that's the expectation for a starting archmaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T21:57:00-07:00","id":1195965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Realmlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system?p=1195856#post1195856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every being I listed is able to be played by an ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> That varies from ST to ST, and you're making quite a stretch to even assume they exist.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, you refer to something that doesn't really exist. You talk about Greater Beings, but there aren't any mechanics for Greater Beings. At 2e, all of those beings exist without any mechanics, for they are gods- so you actually demand the ST to make up mechanics for antagonists other than other archmasters, when they don't actually exist other than a narrative force. It is pointless, because practically you say &quot;archmasters always win&quot;. And you define such Greater Beings through a game paradigm which does not apply to other games, and expect them to either line up or go home. It is not a good game design, IMO- if you take the time to spend about interaction with such Greater Beings, than those Greater Beings should exist mechanically. It sounds like you are trying to be &quot;fair&quot; toward other gamelines, when they could never answer your requirements. You leave too much to the hands of a ST, and lose more than you gain. (and just for the record, the True Fae in 1e do not have Contracts with rating of more than 5 dots. In 2e, they don't have dot rating at all. You practically say &quot;True Fae are Greater Beings&quot; when they don't qualify, and force the ST to make up things on their own if they want to use them. Again, that is not a good design, as you practically have no antagonists in your game other than Archmasters, but spend wordcount on saying that they exist, and you need to make them up on your own.<br /> <br /> And about Luna- the fact that you wrote &quot;it was a titanic battle which lasted a number of days&quot; is written in a way which makes it sound, well, casual- the archmaster in question sounds as if they are eating breakfast, not talking about something which probably had terrible implications upon the whole world. Plus, Luna is, like, a really important character for Forsaken- the way you present it feels like you are sticking a finger in the eye of Werewolf. You practically present the death of one of the most powerful beings in the world as nothing more than a tool to talk about hubristic archmasters, and that it had no consequences whatsoever. Again, it is not a good design. <br /> <br /> In short, IMO, if you talk about Greater Beings as something more than a narrative tool, they should have actual mechanics to support them (which they currently don't. Even high Ranked spirits don't have it in the new edition- but they are at least possible to be translated and don't need to be made up out of scratch- and again, you shouldn't force the game design of one game on others and expect them to hold, especially when you contradict it by listing the Gentry, who don't answer the qualifications, as someone who do) for it is way too much work for a ST to do on their own- and you should be very careful with dealing with references to important characters to other gamelines, for those games have their own fans, and they may not take it very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T21:57:06-07:00","id":1195966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1195582-archmage-the-seeking-2e-homebrew-system?p=1195893#post1195893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's the way you placed it next to the 6th dot. That makes it look like that's the expectation for a starting archmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good catch! <br /> <br /> Anyway, I have a to-do list forming. Too lazy and sick to get everything done tonight. <br /> * Find a better word than &quot;Interdisciplinaries&quot; to describe the subsets of Concepts <br /> * Give more examples to differentiate between Concepts 7 and 8 (Establishments is working &quot;within the system,&quot; modifying what exists; Metamorphoses is wholesale creation and oblivion, unrestrained by what is already real or present. It also has no limits besides the ability and power of the Archmage in question.) <br /> * Concept 9 is doing everything up-to-and-including Metamorphoses, except instead of every spell being an undertaking, it is a prolonged state of power (a scene in game time) where the Archmage can cast freely: it's Ascention-lite. <br /> * Add Archmage &quot;Orders&quot; that are a cross between Cabals and Orders; function very much like Legacies socially. Paragons and Bodhisattvas are staying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T22:09:06-07:00","id":1195968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The thing is, you refer to something that doesn't really exist. You talk about Greater Beings, but there aren't any mechanics for Greater Beings. At 2e, all of those beings exist without any mechanics, for they are gods- so you actually demand the ST to make up mechanics for antagonists other than other archmasters </div> </div> </div>I'm going to try to make this simple for you. Archmages automatically win in a Clash of Wills against anything a player (non-ST) can play.<br /> If you feel up to it, make your own rules for &quot;Greater Beings&quot; - just know that Archmage is the only &quot;Greater Being&quot; that has a book explaining how to play one.<br /> I think you're making mountains out of molehills. If an Archmage needs to CoW against a &quot;god&quot; than it should have some on-the-fly dice pools. Simple as that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And about Luna- the fact that you wrote &quot;it was a titanic battle which lasted a number of days&quot; is written in a way which makes it sound, well, casual- the archmaster in question sounds as if they are eating breakfast, not talking about something which probably had terrible implications upon the whole world. Plus, Luna is, like, a really important character for Forsaken- the way you present it feels like you are sticking a finger in the eye of Werewolf. You practically present the death of one of the most powerful beings in the world as nothing more than a tool to talk about hubristic archmasters, and that it had no consequences whatsoever. Again, it is not a good design. </div> </div> </div>If you think a &quot;titanic battle that lasted for days&quot; sound as casual as eating breakfast, I can't help you. At this point, I think you're deliberately trying to misinterpret.<br /> <br /> As for Luna being important to Werewolves? That's correct. It's also correct that there are a few Archmages out there who have grown stronger than a Rank 8 Spirit, and Archmages are operating on a cosmic scope. Werewolves, regular Mages, Vampires - these little fish are pawns now. Luna (very temporarily) dying may be sad for Werewolves and Spirit Mages alike, but that doesn't mean she's untouchable because Archmage may be stepping on Werewolves proverbial toes. Archmage doesn't step on toes, really - it stomps the whole foot. <br /> <br /> As for consequences? They are always varied - but I'm not writing a book, I wrote a few sentences as flavor text. It's not the end of the world. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 03-16-2018, 01:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T22:29:56-07:00","id":1195973,"title":"","content":"What are/were/will be the consequences of archmages killing gods and each other, not just the Warden Moon, besides getting berated by your peers and ending up with less social standing? Who or what resurrected Luna?<br /> <br /> Maybe what the archmage killed was an Ochema equivalent of the Queen of Shadows, who reigns over only our planet\u2019s moon, and the \u2018true\u2019 Luna resurrected \u2018Earthly\u2019 Luna?<br /> <br /> Granted, this may sound like me getting hung up over trivia... but cosmic trivias are what a game of archmages allow us to indulge in, so pretty please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T23:28:41-07:00","id":1195982,"title":"","content":"In an incident where someone is essentially showing off, there is slightly more lax consequences than, say, truly attempting to erase one of your peers from existence. Remember that the act of killing, in the perspective of Archmages/gods/major Spirits etc, doesn't necessarily mean final. &quot;Final death&quot; is much more serious, as it is the human equivalent of dead.<br /> That said, offing Luna just to show you can is disrespectful to Luna and her cohorts. It's like slapping someone in the face, and wasting their time and resources. In this particular scenario, I'd imagine that the Archmage who killed Luna would be forced to make amends, AND suffer social stigma for hundreds of years (plus always living with that skeleton in your closet). And in a social environment like Archmage, it's crucial to realize that social standing is *everything.* Your world as an Archmage expands, but your social world shrinks dramatically. What your fellow Archmages think of you can make or break you.<br /> <br /> Of course, it takes more than direct combat in any random location to truly kill a Spirit as powerful as Luna. Common knowledge would indicate that the Archmage who killed her wasn't attempting a to really end her existence for good. Think less &quot;whip out a handgun and shoot you in the head&quot; and more &quot;walk up to you and punch your arm to start a fight, then fistfight you until knocking you out.&quot; But it's still something that would garner you a bad reputation. Besides, Luna herself wouldn't necessarily *know* the Archmage wasn't trying to truly kill her; in her perspective, she may have been fighting for her life! Scaring someone that badly is bad form, too.<br /> Also consider that meeting Luna is a big deal. She's not just casually strolling around. What this Archmage did was very intentional -- which makes it all the more gratuitous. <br /> <br /> Then there are those Archmages who truly step over the line. Timelines get reversed and destroyed, histories rewritten, fates respun, new bodies created, people caught in eternally-looping rooms and bottomless pits... bad new bears. Best not violate the Pax too severely.<br /> <br /> And remember: the Pax Arcanum can be applied to beings that are not Archmages if they are aware of it, even if they don't willingly follow it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe what the archmage killed was an Ochema equivalent of the Queen of Shadows, who reigns over only our planet\u2019s moon, and the \u2018true\u2019 Luna resurrected \u2018Earthly\u2019 Luna? </div> </div> </div>That's the problem with gods: once they start replicating themselves, they're hard to pin down. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'd imagine, by the way, that the creation of too many Ochema would be a violation of the Pax. Then again, making 10 is less severe than 50, so that's a good metric to which illustrates the subjective &quot;sliding scale&quot; of severity of breaking the Pax.<br /> <br /> This Archmage fought &quot;Luna.&quot; Whether that means one of Luna's Ochemata fought the &quot;real&quot; Archmage, or one of the Archmage's Ochemata fought the &quot;real&quot; Luna, etc... is for a more detailed story. It could even mean the Archmage and Luna gathered all their Ochema and had a full-on war, less cage match, more World War 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 03-16-2018, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T02:24:16-07:00","id":1195999,"title":"","content":"After reading that, I think that the short episode in the opening post is doing a not so good job at representing the nuances of the games of the gods, which you and at least I agree with. (Except for Luna even possibly having feared the attack, but I digress)<br /> <br /> Heh, now I\u2019m imagining the poor(!) archmage who killed the Queen even once is making amends by sharing Her job as Warden against void-spirits attempting to invade Earth, and keeping the idigam sealed on the moon. If he\u2019s that strong, Father Moon might just decide he\u2019s the perfect partner... or hell, maybe the perfect part-timer to fill in for a century or so, freeing Him to go on a vacation. Maybe some of those greater Lunes aren\u2019t actually spirits at all...<br /> <br /> So, any rules for Ochema/Avatars, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T04:49:07-07:00","id":1196010,"title":"","content":"Casual conversation typically doesn't delve too deeply into nuance; that's what backstory and knowledge of the setting provide. What a casual conversation provides is a glimpse into what ARCHMAGES are thinking. A lack of nuance says something about the perspective of the one saying it.<br /> <br /> Ochema are up-to-and-including perfect clones. At their most powerful, they are exact copies of the Archmaster, who share everything with him: soul, quintessences, mana, abilities, etc. As such, making one with free will and the same level of magical proficiency is paramount to giving birth to a new human (and a new Archmage!) - such an undertaking is not a light decision.<br /> <br /> Much more common is an Ochema with either reduced freedom but full power, or reduced power but full freedom. Archmasters commonly employ Ochema as tools, like a remotely controlled vehicle-clone. Obviously, the practical applications of Ochema are extensive.<br /> <br /> The creation of one, however, is a significant undertaking. As an Imperial Spell, it potentially takes a lot of effort - and besides, no two instances of Imperial Spells are exactly alike, even if you're casting the &quot;same&quot; Ochema spell.<br /> <br /> Avatars are, in my view, what could be considered the Ochema of Ascended Beings. As they have no physical form, Avatars serve that purpose. I could be missing something here, though,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, any rules for Ochema/Avatars, etc? </div> </div> </div>Well I'll throw this out there right away: the death of an Ochema is it's own punishment, as they are each an investment. Also, depending on whether it was free-willed, putting one in danger may risk wisdom decline. The original creator may suffer the same effect as physically dying in The Lie (i.e. Soul Shocked) but this is unconfirmed. Rumor has it that the Archmage must be sharing the Ochema's senses at the time of its death for this to happen - giving the Archmage some incentive to create Ochema which can function on their own and make their own decisions. Archmages known to be cunning and treacherous often make Ochema without free will however, as they fear their own creations will attempt to usurp them. As they saying goes, &quot;evil always turns on itself.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23924,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","user":"Realmlord","date":". 03-16-2018, 07:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23924-realmlord","name":"Realmlord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T06:48:00-07:00","id":1196032,"title":"","content":"Oh, I was referring to Royal Avatars of greater ephemeral entities (and Supernal/Abyssal entities? Not sure if they can spawn Royal Avatars). And I think Ochema of Ascended beings were just called Ochema too.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And while I disagree that archmages would think that way, this is getting into those unsolveable stuff territory, so I\u2019ll drop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 03-16-2018, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}